// X-29/t2, S-1238 (spec §11.3: "束縛の側の `at` は、型注釈の有無によらず構文の段の E0020 で、修正候補はクロックを値の式の全体の後ろへ移す形である"; "束縛の側が `at event` なら式の
// `e at event` の E0815 になるので、候補は束縛の側のクロックを除く形である"): the one candidate of the E0020 of `let w at event = m` takes the clock off the binding side (`let w = m`) and leaves no
// error (`clean`: the candidate that moves the clock to the value, `let w = m at event`, would leave the E0815 of §11.11). The value `w` is the last value of the event `m` at the clock where it is read
// (§11.11), here `sample`. The error is at the `at`. This file has this one error, so `clean` can say it for the whole file; the form with a type annotation (`let w: U32 at event = m`) is in
// flow_clock/e0020_event_binding_clock_s1238.onsa, with the text after the candidate.

pub flow binding_clock_event(m: U32 at event) -> U32 at sample {
  let w at event = m   //~ E0020
  w
}
